Usage: shred [OPTION]... FILE...

Overwrite the specified FILE(s) repeatedly to help prevent data recovery.

OPTIONS:
  -f, --force              ignore write-protection
  -n, --iterations NUM     overwrite N times (default 3)
  -u                       truncate and remove file after overwriting
  -z, --zero               add a final overwrite with zeros to hide shredding
  -v, --verbose            show progress
      --random-source ARG  use FILE as the source of random data
  -s, --size ARG           shred only BYTES bytes instead of the whole file
  -x, --exact              do not round file size up to the next full block
      --remove[=ARG]       truncate and remove FILE after overwriting; HOW can
                           be 'unlink', 'wipe', or 'wipesync'
      --help               display this help and exit
  -V, --version            output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
